Commit:     Aditya Bhatt <bhattadiCS@users.noreply.github.com>
CommitDate: Fri Jul 10 10:09:04 2026 -0400

    fix: pipeline hardening from rigor-audit levers H1/H2/H4/H5/H11/H12
    
    - regrade_traces.py: per-dataset answer_type (arc/gpqa=mcq — running the
      old tool for real would have rewritten ~12,284 correct labels),
      NA-safe reads (literal 'N/A' answers survive), corruption-fragment
      skip. Verified: patched dry-run on the two sentinel cells = 0 flips
      in 33,000 rows.
    - normalize_mcq_answer: '/' guards stop 'N/A' matching as answer 'A'.
    - math sympy fallback: digit-letter products ('0x^2') no longer die as
      broken hex literals; the one genuine label-drift row now grades
      correct. Grader suite 30/30.
    - append_records: strip C0 control chars (except tab/newline) from text
      fields at write time — the CSV row-framing corruption root cause.
    - run_experiment_matrix: analysis_complete() now requires detector
      outputs no older than trace data (prevents the qwen7b_math 75/1500
      staleness class); trace_counts() counts well-formed run_ids only.
    - run_stakes_sweep: harmonize to pipeline utility convention
      lambda*(step-1); report regenerated — boundaries unchanged
      (qwen7b T*=5/7/10 at c=0/10/100), levels uniformly +0.05.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

